# Zenith (CloudResourceOptimizationPlatform) — Cursor Rules

## Startup (Tier A only)

**Every thread / session — read only:**
- `ai-docs/STATUS.md`
- `ai-docs/SCRATCHPAD.md`

**Read `ai-docs/AI_MASTER.md` once per thread** — apply PRE → EXECUTE → POST from memory on later messages. Do not re-open it every turn.

**Never read at startup:** `AUDIT_LOG.md`, `AUDIT_LOG_ARCHIVE_*.md`, `PROGRESS_HISTORY.md`, full `docs/`.

---

## PRE-PHASE (before product code)

**Full** (features, multi-file, API, security, ML): after scope is clear, update **only** `STATUS.md` + `PROGRESS.md` + `SCRATCHPAD.md` with `IN PROGRESS` and `NOT YET DONE` steps. **Do not defer these writes to POST.** Do not add new tracking MD files. Output `📋 PRE-PHASE COMPLETE`.

**Lightweight** (one-file typo/format/tiny fix): Tier A only, one chat line `Lightweight: …`, skip claim rewrite if task unchanged — see `AI_MASTER.md`.

**Continuity:** never EXECUTE with empty/stale `SCRATCHPAD` or empty `PROGRESS` active task while work is in flight.

---

## POST-PHASE (before stop)

**Full:** tests/lint → finalize `STATUS` + `PROGRESS` + `SCRATCHPAD` → append `PROGRESS_HISTORY` → append `AUDIT_LOG` (≤5 bullets) → **`git commit` + `git push`** if anything changed. Chat reply ≤5 bullets + git result.

**Lightweight:** lint/test if needed; commit/push only if you changed files; skip `AUDIT_LOG` / `PROGRESS_HISTORY` unless user asked.

**Git:** mandatory after Full POST when code or `ai-docs/` changed — user does not need to say “push” each time. Skip only if user said “no push” or no file changes.

---

## Anti-waste

- No long session stories in chat or `PROGRESS.md` — use `PROGRESS_HISTORY.md`
- No re-reading `AI_MASTER` or `AUDIT_LOG` each message
- Load `AI_RULES`, `AI_CONTEXT_*`, `DECISIONS` on demand only

---

## Non-negotiables

- Never commit `backend/.env`
- Zero-cost / free-tier — `ai-docs/AI_RULES.md`
- Brand **Zenith** / **ZenithApp**
- Max 2 heavy processes (pytest, npm install, uvicorn, celery)
- Full PRE-PHASE required for security, auth, BYOC, phase work
